A||||15||fierowner||Farty muffler? Exhaust questions!
Z||000000||fierowner||08-18-99||12:08 AM||||I want to replace the ugly tips (factory) on my car with nice new shiny ones. I have an 84 SE 2.5 4 cyl, i think it sounds okay stock, seems to gargle and mumble lowly when i let off the accelerator, which makes me think a glaspack wouldnt sound farty on it.  But it is a 4cyl and i dont want a farty muffler/tips like on the Neons that run around town.  Any recommendations on a muffler? Tips I'll get from a local muffler place probably.  Also, the tailpipe bounces around alot, and makes the car look like something is wrong w/ it. (I get a lot of comments abour that) Can i fix that? or do i need those springs there....(maybe they are just old springs that need replaced) Okay I'm done...thanks!
Z||000001||batboy||08-18-99||08:00 AM||||I personally don't like glasspacks, too loud, calls too much attention to the men in uniforms, and they really don't have enough back pressure for a stock engine (you may actually lose a little bit of low end torque). A turbo style muffler, like the Flowmasters (which are about the best), is a better way to go. They are halfway between the stock mufflers and glasspacks as far as noise goes. They sound much better too. Nice low throaty tone. As for the exhaust bouncing around, it's probably the springs. There are a bunch of springs that hold everything together that get old, rust in two, or just fall off. The bouncing is not good, it constantly flexes the exhaust pipes and fatigues the metal. You may have to do some major exhaust work.
Z||000002||Bruce||08-18-99||08:20 AM||||Check Summit Racing (800-230-3030) for the exhaust tips- they have a good selection of Monza resonators.
Z||000003||fierowner||08-18-99||11:17 PM||||Monza's look great! But they are glasspacks and i dont want farty.  What  about Borla Intercooled Exhaust tips; I saw them in Jegs
